# Observability Service Rules

- Treat observability as best-effort. `recordOperationalEvent()` and notification paths must not break lead, booking, cancellation, CRM, RingCentral, Google Sheets, Granot lifecycle, or cron workflows.
- Use `src/services/observability/index.ts` as the public import surface for instrumentation in other domains.
- Granot Lead Lifecycle Section 33 catalog, closed metric labels, and seven rollout alerts live in [`granotLifecycle.observability.md`](../../docs/knowledge/granot-lifecycle/observability.md). Emit through `recordOperationalEvent()`; keep those event keys and thresholds in `granotLifecycle/` (not `src/config/domain/observability.ts`).
- Resolve all observability Mongoose models through `getObservabilityModel()` / model getters so runtime, production, test, and custom collection modes keep working.
- Keep Mongo/API fields `snake_case`; translate only at response or export boundaries if needed.
- Put observability env policy in `src/config/domain/observability.ts`. Do not scatter `process.env` reads for capture flags, collection names, email mode, recipients, or alert thresholds.
- Rollups are deferred. Do not add `OBSERVABILITY_ROLLUPS_COLLECTION` or assume persisted rollup metrics exist; reports and overview aggregate from events, incidents, notification deliveries, and report runs.
- Incident upserts must dedupe by open/acknowledged fingerprint, increment `count`, refresh latest fields, and only escalate severity (`critical > error > warn`), never downgrade it automatically.
- Notification retries should update the original `NotificationDelivery` logical record in place with `attempt_count`, `last_attempt_at`, and `next_attempt_at`; do not create retry fan-out rows or mark an original failed provider attempt as a separate sent metric.
- Only advance incident notification throttling after `sendNotification()` returns `ok: true`.
- Cron routes stay thin: authenticate with `CRON_SECRET`, call digest/retry services, and record cron failures as operational events without awaiting anything that could block the response unnecessarily.
- Report aggregations that group many rows must `$sort` before `$limit`, then may use deterministic application sorting as a final guard.
- After runtime TypeScript changes in this area, run focused `pnpm test -- src/services/observability/*.test.ts src/config/domain/observability.test.ts` where practical plus `pnpm run typecheck`.
